---
description: AGENTS.md is the rule source and done.md its close-out, which overrides any "don't commit unless asked" protocol
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md), and read [`wiki/home.md`](../../wiki/home.md) first as it says. Folders with rules of their own carry an `AGENTS.md` (`cats/`, `jmri/`, `tools/schematic/`, `ops/hart-ops/`); read it before editing there.

- **Close-out:** the definition of done in [`.claude/commands/done.md`](../../.claude/commands/done.md) overrides the generic Cursor git protocol. When files changed, commit on an `agent/<agent-id>/<topic>` branch, push, and deploy without being asked, unless the user says not to. Never edit in the main checkout: run `make wt TOPIC=<topic> AGENT=cursor` first and open `.claude/worktrees/<topic>/` as the workspace. The guard blocks commits in the main checkout, so edits made there get stranded. `/done` runs it.
- **Docs in the close-out:** step 1 of that file covers the `docs/` summary line and index rerun, status entry length (`wiki/status/`, at most 60 words), the `Status:` line on hand-off pages and `wiki/not-pending.md`.
- **Guard:** [`.cursor/hooks.json`](../hooks.json) runs [`.cursor/hooks/main_guard.py`](../hooks/main_guard.py) before every shell command. It applies the same rules as the Claude Code guard (`.claude/hooks/main_guard.py`); its docstring lists them. Do not work around a deny.
- **MQTT:** never publish to MQTT from an agent, a script launch or a test, even as sample text piped to a tool. Field turnouts are the owner's.
- **Subagents:** the Claude agents in `.claude/agents/` (`panel-tracer`, `repo-auditor`, `site-reviewer`, `archive-researcher`, `site-builder`, `voice-reviewer`, `schematic-builder`, `finding-verifier`, `data-lane`) each hold their scope and read-only rules in the file. A Cursor agent doing the same job follows that file's rules.
